WEBVTT

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.371
Go get it, boy!

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:44.628
So, Leela, how about a romantic ride
in one of those swan boats?

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:47.589
They're kinda dangerous,
but I finally mastered them.

00:00:47.673 --> 00:00:50.175
Those aren't swan boats. They're swans.

00:00:50.259 --> 00:00:52.636
Oh, that explains these boat eggs.

00:00:58.517 --> 00:00:59.601
Whoa!

00:01:04.231 --> 00:01:06.191
Mmm! Hmm...

00:01:07.568 --> 00:01:08.819
Aah!

00:01:21.999 --> 00:01:24.293
Pitiful ballplayers of Earth.

00:01:24.376 --> 00:01:27.087
I am Ethan "Bubblegum" Tate,

00:01:27.171 --> 00:01:30.048
Commander of the Harlem Globetrotters.

00:01:31.425 --> 00:01:33.468
For generations, your puny planet

00:01:33.552 --> 00:01:36.346
has lived in peace
with the Globetrotter home world.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:39.016
But now, for no reason,

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:43.228
we challenge you to defend your honor
on the basketball court.

00:01:44.438 --> 00:01:46.607
Will no one meet our challenge?

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:49.776
Have none of you pathetic Earthlings game?

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:52.154
- What happens if we lose?
- Nothing!

00:01:52.237 --> 00:01:54.656
There is nothing at stake and no threat,

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:56.491
beyond the shame of defeat.

00:02:02.289 --> 00:02:04.917
This will not stand!

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:09.087
I'll take you on, you air-balling bozos!

00:02:09.171 --> 00:02:11.131
You, old man?

00:02:11.215 --> 00:02:13.717
Sweet Clyde, laugh derisively at him.

00:02:18.096 --> 00:02:19.932
I may be an old man,

00:02:20.015 --> 00:02:22.267
in fact, I'm fairly sure I am,

00:02:22.351 --> 00:02:25.604
but I'll put you Globetrotters
in your place

00:02:25.687 --> 00:02:28.732
with my team of mutant atomic supermen!

00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:31.568
Irie, Professor!

00:02:32.569 --> 00:02:36.657
Behold, my mutant atomic supermen!

00:02:38.742 --> 00:02:41.078
They're only a foot high, Professor.

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:45.499
Well, they're still young,
mere atomic superboys, really.

00:02:45.582 --> 00:02:47.459
We'll need to speed up their growth

00:02:47.543 --> 00:02:50.504
with time particles called chronitons.

00:02:50.587 --> 00:02:53.507
Aren't those the particles
that destroyed an entire...

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:54.883
Good news, everyone!

00:02:54.967 --> 00:02:58.428
You're off to the Tempus Nebula
to gather chronitons.

00:03:14.528 --> 00:03:15.946
Hey, Leela, look at me!

00:03:22.369 --> 00:03:25.414
Your face can take a lot of punishment.
That's good to know.

00:03:25.497 --> 00:03:27.708
There's a lot about my face
you don't know.

00:03:27.791 --> 00:03:30.377
Perhaps you and it
could get better acquainted over dinner.

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:32.754
All right. Cool your jets, hotshot.

00:03:32.838 --> 00:03:34.882
Come on, Leela.
Why won't you go out with me?

00:03:34.965 --> 00:03:36.508
We both know there's something there.

00:03:36.592 --> 00:03:40.345
No. I mean cool your jets.
They're melting Bender's face.

00:03:40.429 --> 00:03:43.098
Ow! Oh, my God! Ow!

00:03:46.727 --> 00:03:48.687
Here you go. Hot off the nebula.

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.231
None too soon. While you were gone,

00:03:51.315 --> 00:03:56.028
the Trotters held a news conference
to announce that I was a jive sucker.

00:04:06.747 --> 00:04:07.748
Whoa!

00:04:19.384 --> 00:04:23.305
Behold! My invincible nuclear mutants!

00:04:23.388 --> 00:04:25.265
- Hi.
- Hello.

00:04:26.642 --> 00:04:29.811
Marv Albert here
at Madison Cube Garden

00:04:29.895 --> 00:04:33.440
where the Harlem Globetrotters
take on a squad of atomic supermen

00:04:33.524 --> 00:04:36.527
in what promises
to be a by-the-numbers athletic contest

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:38.904
with no surprises whatsoever.

00:04:40.948 --> 00:04:43.200
There's the tip-off. Globetrotter ball!

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:46.870
Sweet Clyde Dixon to Bubblegum Tate.
Drives down court.

00:04:46.954 --> 00:04:48.914
And Curly Joe from the rear!

00:04:49.206 --> 00:04:51.834
That one grabbed his behindus.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:55.921
Who dares laugh at the jesters of dunk?

00:04:56.004 --> 00:04:58.924
We came to terrify and humiliate you,

00:04:59.007 --> 00:05:00.926
not tickle your funny bones.

00:05:01.009 --> 00:05:03.637
Watch as I embarrass your civilization

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:05.973
by passing the ball to Curly Joe,

00:05:07.891 --> 00:05:11.144
only to have it
remain in my hands with elastic!

00:05:16.108 --> 00:05:19.736
And perhaps this will wipe
the smiles from your faces.

00:05:21.071 --> 00:05:23.949
Goose goes up! Rejected!

00:05:24.032 --> 00:05:25.742
Growtreant from half court.

00:05:25.826 --> 00:05:27.619
Yes!

00:05:31.582 --> 00:05:34.001
Supermen lead, 45-42.

00:05:34.084 --> 00:05:36.086
Arachneon with the steal, to Thorias.

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:38.672
Thorias from downtown.

00:05:38.755 --> 00:05:41.550
Yes! He's really showing us

00:05:41.633 --> 00:05:44.428
what a man with a cannon
in his chest can do.

00:05:44.511 --> 00:05:47.347
No showboating, you atomic hot dog!

00:05:50.434 --> 00:05:54.188
And that's the half,
with the Supermen up 48-42.

00:05:54.271 --> 00:05:56.481
Surprisingly dull so far.

00:06:02.905 --> 00:06:06.241
Bubblegum, the Trotters
are down by six. Reactions?

00:06:06.325 --> 00:06:08.994
It was always our plan
to trail at the half,

00:06:09.077 --> 00:06:11.622
thus deepening
Earth's eventual humiliation.

00:06:11.705 --> 00:06:14.666
Also, what game were the refs watching?

00:06:18.879 --> 00:06:21.423
Curly Joe,
easily amusedby his own antics,

00:06:21.507 --> 00:06:23.509
continues to wreak havoc.

00:06:24.927 --> 00:06:26.845
- What the...
- Hey, man.

00:06:26.929 --> 00:06:28.347
What was that?

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:30.265
Did everything just jump around?

00:06:30.349 --> 00:06:33.644
Or did my brain just stroke off there
for a second?

00:06:33.727 --> 00:06:37.147
Ladies and gentlemen,
something very strange has just happened

00:06:37.231 --> 00:06:41.360
in this basketball game
between space clowns and atomic monsters.

00:06:42.236 --> 00:06:43.237
Hmm?

00:06:49.826 --> 00:06:51.537
Time out! Time out!

00:06:52.746 --> 00:06:53.747
What's happening?

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:56.667
We seem to be lurching forward
randomly in time,

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:59.169
like a needle skipping on a record player.

00:06:59.253 --> 00:07:01.672
What's causing it? Is it my outfit?

00:07:01.755 --> 00:07:03.715
No. It must have something to do

00:07:03.841 --> 00:07:06.718
with those time particles
I used to grow the supermen.

00:07:06.802 --> 00:07:10.514
Time and space
are ripping apart at the seams.

00:07:13.483 --> 00:07:15.360
- Oops.
- Oh, great.

00:07:15.444 --> 00:07:18.697
Now, on top of everything,
we need a new fifth man.

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:20.741
Ooh, ooh, ooh! Put me in, Professor!

00:07:20.824 --> 00:07:22.743
I wanna show Leela my skills.

00:07:22.826 --> 00:07:26.038
Hmm. Will said skills pay the bills?

00:07:26.121 --> 00:07:29.041
Who cares? We're 35 points ahead
with two minutes left.

00:07:29.124 --> 00:07:30.334
What could possibly...

00:07:35.038 --> 00:07:39.334
Globetrotters win 244-86.

00:07:39.418 --> 00:07:41.461
A dark day for humanity, folks.

00:07:41.545 --> 00:07:43.589
We have been beaten

00:07:43.672 --> 00:07:45.507
in basketball.

00:07:45.591 --> 00:07:48.635
Yeah, that's how we do it!

00:07:48.719 --> 00:07:51.513
You are all fools of the highest caliber.

00:07:51.597 --> 00:07:54.892
I don't know what you did, Fry,
but once again, you screwed up.

00:07:54.975 --> 00:07:58.478
Now all the planets are gonna
start crackin' wise about our mamas.

00:07:58.562 --> 00:08:02.274
I'm just glad my fat ugly mama
isn't alive to see this day.

00:08:02.357 --> 00:08:04.818
Enough about your
promiscuous mother, Hermes.

00:08:04.902 --> 00:08:06.403
We have bigger problems.

00:08:06.486 --> 00:08:09.531
This time disruption is extremely serious.

00:08:09.615 --> 00:08:10.991
Damn right, brother man.

00:08:11.074 --> 00:08:15.120
This chronological wang-dang-doodle
could destroy the very matrix of reality.

00:08:15.204 --> 00:08:19.291
- Tate, what do you know about this?
- Not much yet,

00:08:19.374 --> 00:08:22.461
but I am senior lecturer in physics
at Globetrotter U

00:08:22.544 --> 00:08:24.213
and I'd like to help you investigate.

00:08:24.296 --> 00:08:26.423
You're that Bubblegum Tate?

00:08:26.507 --> 00:08:29.885
Well, I sure ain't his grandma.
Now, look here, Prof.

00:08:29.968 --> 00:08:31.094
I think we got ourselves

00:08:31.178 --> 00:08:34.181
an excess of chronitons
in the subatomic interstices.

00:08:34.264 --> 00:08:36.433
Yes. I see.

00:08:36.517 --> 00:08:41.313
Something involving that many big words
could easily destabilize time itself.

00:08:41.396 --> 00:08:43.482
- Is that a problem?
- Indeed so.

00:08:43.565 --> 00:08:46.151
At this rate, by Tuesday
it will be Thursday.

00:08:46.235 --> 00:08:47.945
By Wednesday, it will be August.

00:08:48.028 --> 00:08:51.740
And by Thursday, it will be
the end of existence as we know it.

00:08:52.783 --> 00:08:54.743
I'll have to ask you to clear out now.

00:08:54.826 --> 00:08:57.079
The circus needs to
set up for tomorrow's big...

00:09:06.363 --> 00:09:10.117
Time continues to skip forward randomly.
Details at 11:00.

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:13.996
This is the news at 11:00.
The mysterious and unexplained...

00:09:14.079 --> 00:09:18.667
Turning to entertainment news, teen singer
Wendy might just be the latest...

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:20.669
...won three Grammys last night.

00:09:20.752 --> 00:09:22.921
Found dead in her bathtub.

00:09:23.005 --> 00:09:27.426
Interesting. It's as if we all behave
normally during the time skips,

00:09:27.509 --> 00:09:29.386
but then we have no memory of it.

00:09:29.469 --> 00:09:31.680
- You mean we just...
- My, yes!

00:09:31.763 --> 00:09:34.933
Ooh, just like that. Any luck, Bubblegum?

00:09:35.017 --> 00:09:36.810
Not yet. Listen.

00:09:36.893 --> 00:09:39.021
Don't mind
if I dribble a little while I work.

00:09:39.104 --> 00:09:42.691
Not if you'll grant me
the same liberty.

00:09:42.774 --> 00:09:45.360
Ooh, ooh! Bubblegum, my name's Bender,

00:09:45.444 --> 00:09:48.530
and I'm a huge fan of your work,
both on and off the court.

00:09:48.613 --> 00:09:51.408
- Can I be a Globetrotter?
- Shut up, turkey.

00:09:51.491 --> 00:09:52.576
Ooh.

00:09:52.659 --> 00:09:54.453
Bubblegum, look at this.

00:09:54.536 --> 00:09:58.165
The background time radiation
is fluctuating wildly!

00:09:58.707 --> 00:10:02.627
Good Lord! That sucker's shakin' round
like some fine imported booty!

00:10:02.711 --> 00:10:04.546
Say, I'm no physicist,

00:10:04.629 --> 00:10:07.382
but I think I know
how to stop the skipping. We'll just...

00:10:10.969 --> 00:10:13.180
I don't know how
this was supposed to work.

00:10:13.263 --> 00:10:17.059
Professor, I hope you find out what's
wrong before we skip right past my...

00:10:17.142 --> 00:10:18.727
Happy birthday, Amy!

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:21.438
Hooray! Look at all these presents!

00:10:21.521 --> 00:10:24.524
I hope we all have as much fun
tomorrow at my birth...

00:10:24.608 --> 00:10:25.901
What?

00:10:26.652 --> 00:10:27.903
Oh...

00:10:30.364 --> 00:10:33.825
Psst! Leela! I've set up
a time-proof shelter in the closet.

00:10:33.909 --> 00:10:36.703
There's only room for two,
and I want to share it with you.

00:10:36.787 --> 00:10:39.706
Fry, that's so sweet. Lemme see.

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:47.047
How exactly
will this protect us from time jumps?

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:51.134
'Cause when we're together in here,
baby, time will stand still.

00:10:51.635 --> 00:10:52.636
Ow!

00:10:54.545 --> 00:10:55.546
Hmm.

00:10:56.390 --> 00:10:57.391
Hmm.

00:11:00.185 --> 00:11:03.063
Dr. Zoidberg, can I talk to you about Fry?

00:11:03.146 --> 00:11:05.065
Leela, I would be honored.

00:11:05.148 --> 00:11:07.025
...does the worst

00:11:07.109 --> 00:11:08.986
W.C. Fields imitation I've ever seen.

00:11:09.069 --> 00:11:10.570
- Zoidberg!
- Sorry.

00:11:10.654 --> 00:11:12.948
You must've been boring me.

00:11:13.031 --> 00:11:17.327
The thing is, Fry is very sweet,
but he's so immature.

00:11:17.411 --> 00:11:21.123
I love his boyish charm,
but I hate his childishness.

00:11:21.206 --> 00:11:22.916
So he's not perfect.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:26.753
You don't wanna end up
old and lonely like Zoidberg.

00:11:30.465 --> 00:11:31.842
You were saying?

00:11:34.136 --> 00:11:37.180
Ah, there it is. The Tempus Nebula.

00:11:37.264 --> 00:11:39.349
Take a whiff through the Smell-A-Scope.

00:11:41.810 --> 00:11:44.021
Ooh, what's that funky jazz?

00:11:44.104 --> 00:11:46.690
The odor of pure time leaking.

00:11:46.773 --> 00:11:48.942
When my crew removed the chronitons,

00:11:49.026 --> 00:11:50.861
it destabilized the nebula,

00:11:50.944 --> 00:11:53.405
causing time skips
throughout the universe.

00:11:53.488 --> 00:11:55.532
Ooh, let Bubblegum tell it!

00:11:55.615 --> 00:11:59.077
Pretend these basketballs
are time particles, my silver honky.

00:11:59.161 --> 00:12:01.413
As the nebula bounce-passes them off us...

00:12:01.496 --> 00:12:02.789
Ow! Ooh! Aah!

00:12:02.873 --> 00:12:05.667
...they cause these dents,
or "time skips."

00:12:05.751 --> 00:12:07.878
You are so smart.

00:12:07.961 --> 00:12:10.964
Hold up. What if we were
to move this cluster of stars

00:12:11.048 --> 00:12:13.383
to these algebraic coordinates?

00:12:13.467 --> 00:12:16.219
Their gravity might just
divert the chronitons

00:12:16.303 --> 00:12:18.221
to the empty side of the universe.

00:12:18.305 --> 00:12:20.891
Yeah. But it's impossible.

00:12:20.974 --> 00:12:23.977
Moving stars would require
one bad-ass gravity pump.

00:12:24.061 --> 00:12:26.063
And we'd need all the money
on Earth to build...

00:12:26.146 --> 00:12:27.272
- What the...
- Whoa! What?

00:12:29.691 --> 00:12:31.902
There's the funding for your gravity pump.

00:12:31.985 --> 00:12:33.528
But it damn well better work.

00:12:33.612 --> 00:12:36.198
We can't spend all
of Earth's money every day.

00:12:36.281 --> 00:12:38.450
Now, how long will it take to build?

00:12:38.533 --> 00:12:42.913
It won't be easy, Nixon. A jim-jam
this complex might take months or even...

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:45.123
Ah, there we are.

00:12:45.207 --> 00:12:49.836
One gravity pump powerful enough
to move the stars themselves.

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:53.840
Now to begin the arduous task
of attaching it to the ship so...

00:12:56.301 --> 00:12:58.220
Off you go, apparently.

00:13:04.351 --> 00:13:08.188
Easy, Leela. Just finger-roll
that star into the cosmic basket.

00:13:09.189 --> 00:13:11.942
Just a few more

00:13:12.025 --> 00:13:16.405
hundred thousand miles.

00:13:16.488 --> 00:13:17.531
There.

00:13:22.035 --> 00:13:23.912
Nothin' but nebula.

00:13:23.996 --> 00:13:26.206
We'll have to run some tests
back on Earth,

00:13:26.289 --> 00:13:28.333
but I think we've stopped the time skips.

00:13:28.417 --> 00:13:29.418
- All right!
- Jammin'!

00:13:29.501 --> 00:13:30.711
Hooray for Leela!

00:13:30.794 --> 00:13:32.963
And what better way
to celebrate our success

00:13:33.046 --> 00:13:36.925
than by me showing Bubblegum
the Globetrotter uniform I made myself.

00:13:37.009 --> 00:13:38.427
Lemme see.

00:13:39.636 --> 00:13:41.138
Hello, lawsuit.

00:13:41.221 --> 00:13:43.181
Leela, I want you to know

00:13:43.265 --> 00:13:46.685
I think the way you moved
those stars around was really wonderful.

00:13:46.768 --> 00:13:48.395
I got you something.

00:13:49.104 --> 00:13:52.482
Moderately priced
domestic non-vintage champagne!

00:13:52.566 --> 00:13:53.734
How did you know?

00:13:53.817 --> 00:13:58.363
You deserve it. I mean, nobody ever stops
to tell you what a great captain you are.

00:13:58.447 --> 00:14:01.074
Aw, that is so true and sweet.

00:14:01.158 --> 00:14:03.035
You're smart, you're beautiful,

00:14:03.118 --> 00:14:05.662
and best of all, you'll go out with me?

00:14:05.746 --> 00:14:08.749
Fry, please try to understand.

00:14:08.832 --> 00:14:12.294
You're a man. I'm a woman.
We're just too different.

00:14:12.377 --> 00:14:14.338
Hey, Leela! Bubblegum might let me

00:14:14.421 --> 00:14:17.299
organize a bake sale
for the Globetrotter wives.

00:14:17.382 --> 00:14:19.468
Can you teach me to make cupcakes?

00:14:19.551 --> 00:14:22.721
All right, but I wanna lick the beaters.

00:14:22.804 --> 00:14:24.848
I got her champagne. I opened it.

00:14:24.931 --> 00:14:26.683
What does a guy have to do?

00:14:26.767 --> 00:14:29.019
Eighty-six the chump stuff, F-man.

00:14:29.102 --> 00:14:34.358
It's time to win Leela's heart with a big,
showy, three-point romantic gesture.

00:14:34.441 --> 00:14:38.820
Hmm. Maybe this is the moment
to show her my real surprise.

00:14:43.283 --> 00:14:45.202
Fry, what are you doing?

00:14:45.285 --> 00:14:48.080
Uh-oh. Time to boogie on
down to the sauna.

00:14:48.872 --> 00:14:51.416
Look. I've been studying
how to pilot the ship.

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:54.169
- Impressed?
- Yeah, actually.

00:14:54.252 --> 00:14:57.673
You're doing okay.
The core-reactor temperature's nominal.

00:14:57.756 --> 00:14:58.757
The blinker's off.

00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:00.550
I learned how to work the gravity pump

00:15:00.634 --> 00:15:02.469
in case we need to move more stars.

00:15:02.552 --> 00:15:03.762
So, are we dating now?

00:15:03.845 --> 00:15:08.475
Is that what this is all about?
Please, just cut it out now.

00:15:08.558 --> 00:15:10.977
Look, Leela. I know there's some perfect,

00:15:11.061 --> 00:15:13.438
amazing thing I can do
to make you love me.

00:15:13.522 --> 00:15:16.233
- And when I figure out what it is...
- Fry, stop.

00:15:16.316 --> 00:15:20.529
I don't wanna hurt you,
but there is absolutely, positively no way

00:15:20.612 --> 00:15:23.156
that you and I will ever, ever...

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:26.785
...man and wife.
You may kiss the bride.

00:15:26.868 --> 00:15:28.912
Mmm...

00:15:31.123 --> 00:15:32.124
Yes!

00:15:37.838 --> 00:15:39.798
He looks radiant.

00:15:41.049 --> 00:15:43.301
Ye gods, Bubblegum! We failed.

00:15:43.385 --> 00:15:45.512
The time skips haven't stopped at all.

00:15:45.595 --> 00:15:49.057
Even in these formal shorts,
I feel like a failure.

00:15:49.141 --> 00:15:51.560
You tricked me
into marrying you, didn't you?

00:15:51.643 --> 00:15:52.769
Of course not!

00:15:52.853 --> 00:15:55.689
How'd you do it?
Drugs in the champagne? Hypnosis?

00:15:55.772 --> 00:15:57.774
No! Drugs are for losers!

00:15:57.858 --> 00:16:00.819
And hypnosis is for losers
with big weird eyebrows.

00:16:00.902 --> 00:16:03.864
I don't know what amazing thing
I did to make you love me,

00:16:03.947 --> 00:16:06.033
but whatever it was, we're married now.

00:16:06.116 --> 00:16:08.285
We've got the rest
of our lives to work this...

00:16:08.368 --> 00:16:11.038
- ...divorce is final.
- What?

00:16:11.121 --> 00:16:13.123
Well, let's divide up the china.

00:16:13.206 --> 00:16:17.419
I guess I'll take the NFC helmets
and you can have the AFC helmets.

00:16:17.502 --> 00:16:20.088
Fine. Break my heart again.

00:16:20.213 --> 00:16:22.716
Don't be so hard on yourself, Fry.

00:16:22.799 --> 00:16:24.760
You lost the woman of your dreams,

00:16:24.843 --> 00:16:26.803
but you still have Zoidberg.

00:16:26.887 --> 00:16:29.097
You all still have Zoidberg!

00:16:29.181 --> 00:16:32.184
How did I do it?
How did I get Leela to love me?

00:16:32.267 --> 00:16:33.894
I've got to figure it out.

00:16:33.977 --> 00:16:36.438
Maybe you're just a fantastic lover, Fry.

00:16:36.521 --> 00:16:38.231
- Um, no.
- I don't know what I'm doing.

00:16:38.315 --> 00:16:41.652
Maybe she'd come back to you if your
best friend, Bender, were a Globetrotter.

00:16:41.735 --> 00:16:43.737
- What do you say, Bubblegum?
- Hell no.

00:16:44.112 --> 00:16:45.197
Oh...

00:16:45.280 --> 00:16:46.823
Oh, it's hopeless.

00:16:46.907 --> 00:16:49.826
I did something so great
that it won Leela's heart,

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:52.245
and I'll never ever know what it was.

00:16:52.329 --> 00:16:53.664
My life is empty.

00:16:55.290 --> 00:16:57.709
Zoidberg...

00:16:57.793 --> 00:17:00.545
No wonder we failed
to stop the time skips.

00:17:00.629 --> 00:17:03.924
Diverting chronitons
is mathematically impossible.

00:17:04.007 --> 00:17:08.136
I knew I should've checked
your showboating Globetrotter algebra.

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:11.390
Man, I thought you knew
that algebra was all razzmatazz!

00:17:11.473 --> 00:17:15.102
A Globetrotter always saves
the good algebra for the final minutes.

00:17:15.227 --> 00:17:17.938
Vintage Bubblegum!

00:17:18.021 --> 00:17:20.190
The time skips are worse than ever now.

00:17:20.273 --> 00:17:24.152
Isolated spots are jumping
by years at a time. Look!

00:17:24.236 --> 00:17:26.279
Stupid senior citizens.

00:17:26.363 --> 00:17:29.366
Why should we have to pay
for their Social Security benefits?

00:17:29.449 --> 00:17:31.868
I deserve free money!

00:17:31.952 --> 00:17:34.037
Well, I'm stumped.

00:17:34.121 --> 00:17:37.541
We'll have to call in the finest
scientific minds in the universe...

00:17:38.417 --> 00:17:41.670
Perhaps we could explode
the whole damned nebula.

00:17:41.753 --> 00:17:44.756
- What do you think, Curly Joe?
- No, man.

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:49.052
An explosion big enough to destroy that
mama would take out half the universe.

00:17:49.136 --> 00:17:52.180
You gotta Globetrotter
that explosion up a little, Farnsie.

00:17:52.264 --> 00:17:54.349
Make it an implosion.

00:17:54.433 --> 00:17:56.935
By God, Sweet Clyde is right!

00:17:57.019 --> 00:17:59.855
An implosion might just form a black hole

00:17:59.938 --> 00:18:02.399
that would stop
more chronitons from escaping.

00:18:02.482 --> 00:18:05.652
Whoa! Slow that brain train down, Prof!

00:18:05.736 --> 00:18:09.156
We'd need some kind of doomsday device
to initiate an implosion like that.

00:18:09.239 --> 00:18:11.158
Doomsday device?

00:18:11.241 --> 00:18:15.662
Ah, now the ball's in Farnsworth's court!

00:18:18.707 --> 00:18:22.085
I suppose I could part with one
and still be feared.

00:18:22.169 --> 00:18:24.087
Gimme some skin, Prof.

00:18:24.171 --> 00:18:26.298
I'm making you an honorary Globetrotter.

00:18:26.381 --> 00:18:30.135
In fact, everybody in this room's
an honorary Globetrotter.

00:18:30.218 --> 00:18:32.179
- Yay!
- I'm a Globetrotter!

00:18:33.597 --> 00:18:35.057
Did you just say...

00:18:35.140 --> 00:18:37.726
- Too late, hot plate.
- Aw, crap!

00:18:42.981 --> 00:18:45.734
We must leave now,
for we are needed elsewhere.

00:18:45.817 --> 00:18:48.153
But we wish you Godspeed.

00:18:50.656 --> 00:18:52.616
Please! Please let me come with you.

00:18:52.699 --> 00:18:54.534
I can make myself taller.

00:18:56.370 --> 00:18:59.206
Bender, you can talk trash.
You can handle the ball.

00:18:59.289 --> 00:19:01.416
But look in your heart and ask yourself,

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:04.419
are you funky enough to be a Globetrotter?

00:19:04.503 --> 00:19:06.755
- Are you?
- Yes.

00:19:06.838 --> 00:19:10.759
- Are you?
- I mean, with time, my funk level could...

00:19:10.842 --> 00:19:13.512
- Are you?
- No.

00:19:13.595 --> 00:19:15.347
Deal with it.

00:19:31.146 --> 00:19:33.398
Oh! No!

00:19:33.481 --> 00:19:36.234
Careful with that doomsday device, Bender.

00:19:36.318 --> 00:19:39.321
What does it matter?
I'll never be a Globetrotter.

00:19:39.404 --> 00:19:43.200
My life, and by extension
everyone else's, is meaningless.

00:19:43.283 --> 00:19:44.284
Roger.

00:19:45.110 --> 00:19:46.904
Leela, about the wedding...

00:19:46.987 --> 00:19:49.114
I don't know what I did
to make you love me,

00:19:49.197 --> 00:19:52.367
and I don't think
I tricked you into it, but maybe I did.

00:19:52.451 --> 00:19:54.828
And if I did, I'm sorry.

00:19:54.912 --> 00:19:58.874
It's okay, Fry. You know
we'll always be friends, right?

00:19:58.957 --> 00:20:01.418
Yeah, but I don't guess
anything I could do

00:20:01.501 --> 00:20:04.796
will ever make you feel
the same way about me that I do about you.

00:20:04.880 --> 00:20:06.089
I guess not.

00:20:10.469 --> 00:20:13.096
Well, the doomsday device is ready.

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:15.432
Maybe blasting this quadrant of space

00:20:15.515 --> 00:20:19.061
into a hellstorm of flaming nothingness
will cheer me up a little.

00:20:19.144 --> 00:20:22.272
Okay. Let me just
take the ship out to a safe distance.

00:20:24.524 --> 00:20:28.237
Actually, I think I'll go down
and prep the detonator.

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:30.906
Fry, why don't you take the helm?

00:20:35.494 --> 00:20:38.789
She's so great.
I feel like I can almost remember

00:20:38.872 --> 00:20:41.250
the magical thing I did
to make her love me.

00:20:41.333 --> 00:20:43.252
But I guess I never will.

00:20:43.335 --> 00:20:48.757
Sorry, buddy. I, too, know what it's like
to have a dream I'll never achieve.

00:21:01.520 --> 00:21:02.896
Oh...

00:21:10.112 --> 00:21:12.114
That's how I must've done it!

00:21:12.197 --> 00:21:16.577
I moved the stars themselves
to write her a love note in the sky!

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:20.080
Detonation in three, two, one.

00:21:20.163 --> 00:21:23.792
No!

00:21:33.218 --> 00:21:35.262
Did you see it? Did you see it?

00:21:35.345 --> 00:21:38.181
- The explosion?
- No, not the explosion!

00:21:38.265 --> 00:21:40.017
Then what?

00:21:41.310 --> 00:21:42.352
Nothing.